{{Quote|Are we safe here?''"<br />"''You're a new test pilot. You've just arrived, you're excited. You wanted to look around before you went to bed. We started flirting.''"<br />"''I like that.|Cassian Andor and Niya|audio=Andor-Niya-Flirting-OneYearLater.flac|<ref name="One Year Later" />}}
'''Sienar TF73''', or just '''Sienar''' or '''73''', was a [[Water|snow]]-covered [[planet]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Tharin sector]] that was owned by [[Sienar Fleet Systems]]. One of many numbered worlds owned by the company, 73 was home to [[Sienar Test Facility 73]]. A [[TIE Avenger prototype]] was kept there and inspected by the [[technician]] [[Niya]]. In [[4 BBY]], Niya helped the [[Axis network|rebel]] [[spy]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|infiltrate]] the facility to steal the prototype. After prepping the TIE Avenger for a test flight, she briefed the spy, who reassured her about her sacrifice.

Andor proceeded to board the TIE Avenger and try to fly it out of the facility. Difficulty with the unfamiliar controls delayed the spy, who was forced to fight off facility security before he could break out. He was pursued by two [[TIE/ad v1]]s through 73's canyons and ultimately destroyed his pursuers with falling debris before escaping offworld.

==Description==
[[File:Sienar-TF73-SWmap.png|thumb|left|300px|Sienar TF73 lay along the Triellus Trade Route.]]
Sienar TF73,<ref name="Galaxy">{{StarWarsGalaxyMap}}</ref> also known as simply Sienar<ref name="One Year Later" /> or 73,<ref name="Databank" /> was a terrestrial<ref name="One Year Later" /> [[planet]]<ref name="Databank" /> located in an [[Sienar TF73 system|eponymous star system]] within an intersecting portion of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Systems" /> and [[the Slice]].<ref name="Slice" /> Situated in the [[Tharin sector]] at the coordinates S-8 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Systems" /> it lay along the [[Triellus Trade Route]]<ref name="Triellus" /> between the [[Jabiim system|Jabiim]] and [[Yarma system]]s.<ref name="Galaxy" /> The world was at least partially covered with a [[Temperature|frozen]] landscape that included [[Water|glaciers]]. It featured snow-covered [[mountain]]s and canyons on the land and an [[ocean]] with icebergs. The climate was frigid with winds.<ref name="One Year Later" />

==History==
===Security breach===
{{Quote|How's it look?''"<br />"''It's good. It's prepped for a test flight in the morning. The password tonight is Kafrene.|Cassian Andor and Niya|<ref name="One Year Later" />}}
[[File:Niya-TIEAvenger-OneYearLater.png|thumb|right|300px|Niya was assigned to the TIE Avenger prototype's upkeep.]]
By the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], Sienar TF73 was one of many numbered worlds owned by<ref name="Databank" /> the [[starship]] manufacturing company<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> [[Sienar Fleet Systems]]. There, the company housed [[Sienar Test Facility 73]], which contained many Imperial secrets and was subsequently defended by its own [[Sienar Test Facility 73 defense battalion|battalion]].<ref name="Databank" /> The facility's security operated without a fixed roster, to the dislike of some, though fear of being reassigned kept them from speaking up.<ref name="One Year Later" /> As the Empire expanded its [[Imperial Navy]],<ref name="Starfighters2">[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles (second edition)|''Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles'', second edition]]</ref> Imperial [[engineer]]s seeking to improve<ref name="Avenger DB">{{Databank|tie-avenger-prototype|TIE Avenger prototype}}</ref> Sienar Fleet System's<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighter]] developed<ref name="Avenger DB" /> the [[TIE Avenger prototype]] at the facility.<ref name="Starfighters2" /> The Sienar [[technician]]<ref name="Inside Season 2">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-interview-tony-gilroy|text=Making a Revolutionary: Inside ''Andor'' Season 2 with Tony Gilroy}}</ref> [[Niya]] was assigned to the prototype's upkeep.<ref name="Niya DB">{{Databank|niya|Niya}}</ref> However, despite having enjoyed her job, she communicated with<ref name="One Year Later" /> an [[Axis network|anti-Imperial network]] secretly coordinated by the rebel [[agent]] [[Luthen Rael]].<ref name="DOR Guide">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> A plan was formed by the network to steal the TIE Avenger prototype with the help of Niya.<ref name="One Year Later" />

The rebel [[spy]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|infiltrated]] Sienar Test Facility 73 in [[4 BBY]], disguised as an [[Imperial Starfighter Pilot|Imperial test pilot]]. While Andor waited to meet Niya, she prepped the prototype for a test flight the next morning. She met with the spy for the first time, briefing him on the situation of the TIE Avenger, giving him the password and credentials to access the fighter, and producing a cover story for their conversation. The technician was nervous about the mission, but Andor reassured her about her sacrifice. The pair were briefly interrupted by a [[Niya's coworker|coworker]] of Niya, and the technician gave the cover story to her colleague before the latter moved along. Niya asked Andor if it was worth it if she died that night, the spy reassuring her that her decision to help the fight against the Empire made it worth it already. After thanking him, the technician asked for a twelve-[[Standard minute|minute]] head start. Andor agreed and the two parted ways.<ref name="One Year Later" />

===To steal a TIE===
{{Quote|I need a twelve minute head start.''"<br />"''Is that enough?''"<br />[Niya nods]<br />''"I'll see you along the road.|Niya and Cassian Andor|audio=Niya-Andor-Headstart-OneYearLater.flac|<ref name="One Year Later" />}}
Andor soon made his way to the TIE Avenger's hangar and used Niya's credentials to open the hangar doors. He shot a [[droid]] stationed there before climbing into the prototype. Unfamiliar with the controls, the spy attempted to fly the TIE Avenger out of the hangar, only to reverse it by accident and start crashing into the walls and ceiling. The commotion sounded the station alarms, and the hangar doors closed as a complement of [[stormtrooper]]s arrived to attend to the situation. The stormtroopers fired on the prototype, but Andor quickly figured out how to let loose the fighter's rotary [[laser cannon]]s on them, quickly dispatching the troopers. A [[range trooper]] armed with a [[Smart Rocket]] attempted to flank and destroy the TIE Avenger, but Andor evaded the first rocket and eliminated the trooper with a special, high-powered [[laser cannon]] on the prototype.<ref name="One Year Later" />

[[File:TIE-chase-Andor201.png|thumb|left|300px|TIE Advanced v1s pursue Cassian Andor between 73's glaciers.]]
Andor blasted his way out of the hangar in the TIE Avenger, which initially slid across 73's icy surface to the edge of a canyon cliff, where it lost power. Two [[TIE/ad v1]]s,<ref name="One Year Later" /> another prototype model from Sienar Fleet Systems,<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> were deployed to deal with the rebel spy. While the Avenger prototype was restoring power to its systems, the TIE Advanced fighters each fired a [[torpedo]]. However, Andor was able to take off and evade them before descending into the canyon. The two TIE Advanced v1s pursued and fired on the TIE Avenger as the rebel spy struggled to maneuver it. The chase made its way between multiple glaciers and towards a glacial tunnel. Andor fired four torpedoes at the glacier, causing the tunnel to collapse as he flew through with his pursuers. The two TIE Advanced v1s were crushed by the collapse, allowing Andor to escape Sienar TF73 in the stolen TIE Avenger to return to his [[Porko|contact]] on<ref name="One Year Later" /> the [[moon]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> [[Yavin 4]].<ref name="Sagrona Teema">{{Andor|Sagrona Teema}}</ref>

==Locations==
{{Quote|I&hellip; I've had fun here. That must sound strange.''"<br />"''No, not at all.|Niya and Cassian Andor|<ref name="One Year Later" />}}
On 73 was Sienar Test Facility 73, which was ran by Sienar Fleet Systems and housed Imperial secrets<ref name="Databank" /> like the TIE Avenger prototype. An illuminated open road ran from the facility to another lit location on the planet.<ref name="One Year Later" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Tie_avenger_bts.png|thumb|right|300px|The set of the hangar on 73 at Pinewood Studios]]
Sienar TF73 first appeared as just "Sienar" in "[[One Year Later]]," the first episode of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'',<ref name="One Year Later" /> which aired on [[Disney+]] on [[April 22]], [[2025]].<ref name="S2 Companion">{{InsiderCite|233|Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion}}</ref> It was initially teased in the first trailer for the season, posted on the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] channel on [[February 24]] of that year.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|AE4wxt70aUM|Andor &#124; Season 2 Trailer &#124; Streaming April 22 on Disney+}}</ref> The world was identified as "73" in a [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry about the Sienar Test Facility 73 located there, which was published by the day after the release of "One Year Later."<ref name="Databank" /> It was identified in an [[October 13]], 2025 update<ref name="Substack">{{Substack|subdomain=jasonfry|url=p/star-wars-galaxy-map-update|text=Star Wars Galaxy Map Update|name=[[Jason Fry]]|username=jasonfry|date=2025-10-13}}</ref> to the [[Star Wars Galaxy Map|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map]] on StarWars.com,<ref name="Systems" /> authored by [[Jason Fry]].<ref name="Substack">{{Substack|subdomain=jasonfry|url=p/star-wars-galaxy-map-update|text=Star Wars Galaxy Map Update|name=[[Jason Fry]]|username=jasonfry|date=2025-10-13}}</ref>

Concept art for 73 was created by [[Randolph Watson]].<ref name="Concept">{{SW|url=news/andor-concept-to-screen|text=Taking ''Andor'' from Concept to Screen}}</ref> The hangar scenes on the planet were filmed at [[Pinewood Studios]].<ref name="ILM Avenger">{{ILM|url=andor-star-wars-tie-avenger-ilm-vfx|text=Assembling a Starfighter: Exploring ILM's Role in Creating the TIE Avenger from 'Andor'}}</ref> [[Industrial Light & Magic]] (ILM) used visual effects to model the planet's landscape and the action sequences on it. It showed some of the processes of its visual effects in a video presenting its work for the consideration of an Emmy nomination.<ref name="ILM FYC">{{ILMVFXYouTube|vCckxCitIC0|Behind the Magic &#124; The Visual Effects of ANDOR &#124; FYC|date=2025-06-19}}</ref> Indeed, ILM earned a nomination for "Special Visual Effects in a Season or a Movie," one of fourteen nominations the season received,<ref name="">{{ILM|url=emmy-nominations-ilm-visual-effects-rings-power-severance-andor|text=ILM Earns 3 Emmy Nominations for 'Andor,' 'Rings of Power,' and 'Severance'}}</ref> and the company went on to win the award at the [[Wikipedia:77th Primetime Creative Arts Emmy Awards|77th Primetime Creative Arts Emmy Awards]].<ref name="Emmy win">{{WebCite|url=https://www.televisionacademy.com/awards/nominees-winners/2025/outstanding-special-visual-effects-in-a-season-or-a-movie|text=Nominees & Winners: Outstanding Special Visual Effects In A Season Or A Movie|work=the [https://www.televisionacademy.com/ Television Academy website]|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/kk2Xd}}</ref>

